MEMORANDUM

To: TechVentures Board of Directors
From: Sarah Chen, Chief Executive Officer
Date: January 5, 2026
Subject: Q4 2025 Leadership Update

Dear Board Members,

I am pleased to announce the following leadership appointments effective January 1, 2026:

EXECUTIVE APPOINTMENTS

Marcus Williams has been promoted to Chief Technology Officer, reporting directly to me. Marcus previously served as Vice President of Engineering since 2022, where he led the successful migration of our portfolio monitoring platform to cloud infrastructure and grew the engineering team from 200 to 500 employees. His deep technical expertise and proven leadership make him the ideal choice for this expanded role.

Dr. Amira Hassan joins TechVentures as Chief Data Officer. Dr. Hassan comes to us from DataScale Inc, where she served as Head of AI Platform for the past four years. At DataScale, she built and led a team of 45 data scientists and engineers. She holds a PhD in Computer Science from MIT and has published extensively on knowledge graph systems. Dr. Hassan will report to Marcus Williams and will be responsible for all data infrastructure, analytics, and AI initiatives across TechVentures and our portfolio companies.

James O'Brien continues as Chief Financial Officer. James joined TechVentures in 2019 and has been instrumental in our growth. His team has expanded to 12 people following the acquisition of FinanceHub's back-office operations in November 2025. James oversees all financial operations, investor relations, and portfolio company financial oversight.

ORGANIZATIONAL UPDATE

Our engineering organization now comprises 847 employees across three locations:
- San Francisco (Headquarters): 512 employees
- Austin Technology Center: 203 employees  
- London Engineering Office: 132 employees

We have also opened a small research office in Toronto with 15 employees focused on AI safety research, reporting to Dr. Hassan.

I look forward to discussing these changes at our next board meeting on January 15, 2026.

Respectfully,

Sarah Chen
Chief Executive Officer
TechVentures
